# {{.Name}}

An agent scaffolded by `microagent init` ({{.Provider}}). It reads a
`WorkRequest` from `/workspace/input.json`, runs an agentic loop with `bash`,
`read_file`, and `write_file` tools that execute inside the microVM's
`/workspace`, and writes a `WorkResult` to `/workspace/result.json`. Lifecycle
signals stream to stderr as JSON lines.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `microagent.yaml` | Workspace spec: image, setup, entrypoint, files, outputs. |
| `agent.py` | The agent — the loop you edit. |
| `protocol.py` | Request/reply wire shapes (shaped by the ASK framework). Stable; rarely edited. |
| `demo/constraints.json` | Operator-owned constraint envelope, baked in at `/agent/constraints.json`. |
| `demo/system_prompt.md` | System prompt, baked in at `/agent/system_prompt.md`. |
| `demo/` | A library of sample `WorkRequest`s, delivered per run as `/workspace/input.json` — see [`demo/README.md`](demo/README.md). |

## Run it

You'll need an API key in `{{.APIKeyEnv}}`. From this directory:

```sh
# 1. Create the workspace from the spec (pulls the image, builds the rootfs,
#    runs setup). The CLI passes the key as an env var so it stays out of the spec.
microagent create --file microagent.yaml --env {{.APIKeyEnv}}=${{.APIKeyEnv}}

# 2. Deliver a request (the one thing that changes per run).
microagent cp demo/input-001.json {{.Name}}:/workspace/input.json

# 3. Start it, then read the structured result.
microagent start {{.Name}}
microagent --json status {{.Name}}   # poll until the result is ready
microagent --json result {{.Name}}
```

The workspace persists between starts — halt it, deliver a new request with
`microagent cp`, and start it again; the agent can read whatever it wrote before.

## Edit it

Start with `agent.py` — swap the model, add tools, or change `process()`. Keep
the `WorkResult` shape from `protocol.py` so the structured `result` output and
downstream mediation stay stable.
